virtio-gpu: suspend to RAM and resume (arche-os T5)

Linux 6.12's virtio-gpu has no freeze and restore. Suspended to RAM in
QEMU, the device is reset as the machine wakes, and virtio-pci resets it
on resume besides: its queues are gone, and the host's resources with
them. The driver goes on queueing into the dead queue, and once that is
full the next screen update waits for room forever.

Here, before suspending, the outputs are turned off, the queues drained
and deleted; on resume the queues are found again, every classic 2D
resource is made again on the host under its id with its pages attached,
and the outputs turned on as they were, which transfers what they show.
Linux after 6.12 has freeze and restore of its own, which make the
resources again only after hibernation.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_drv.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <drm/drm_drv.h>
 #include <drm/drm_fbdev_shmem.h>
 #include <drm/drm_file.h>
